{
  "_doc": "Feature manifest for verify_all.py. Each feature lists how its tests are recognised per layer: `rust` = test-path prefixes (module::submodule; the longest matching prefix across features wins, as for `vitest`), `vitest` = file-path prefixes, `e2e` = sweep feature names or `Feature/step` regexes, `oracle` = tagboard_check kinds, `evals` = case-id regexes, `contract` = rust/vitest name regexes (vitest: matched against the file path; `src/lib/apiContract/<feature>.api.test.ts` holds each feature's api.ts ↔ Rust command contract) that count as contract tests instead of unit tests. `integration_names` = keywords looked up in an integration test's name, first feature in file order wins. Unmatched tests land in `Transversal`.",
